==============================================================================
3b. The hazard the suite has no clause for: two workers, one thread
==============================================================================
  distinct writers on thread: ['anonymous', 'worker-A-LIVE', 'worker-B-ZOMBIE']
  writes accepted after a 2nd writer appeared: 3
  latest checkpoint id: 1f1a3dfb-b095-66e6-bfff-8258de61006f
  pending_writes now:   [('3523557d-bb47-4022-8902-fffd2b619226', 'ch', 'B-work')]
  Both workers' state coexists. NO conformance clause forbids this,
  and no error type exists for the saver to signal a refusal.

==============================================================================
3c. Is there an error type the runtime treats specially?
==============================================================================
  langgraph.errors.__all__ = ('EmptyChannelError', 'ErrorCode', 'GraphDrained', 'GraphRecursionError', 'InvalidUpdateError', 'GraphBubbleUp', 'GraphInterrupt', 'NodeCancelledError', 'NodeError', 'NodeInterrupt', 'NodeTimeoutError', 'ParentCommand', 'EmptyInputError', 'TaskNotFound')
    CheckpointNotLatest  present=False
    CheckpointRejected   present=False
    FencedOut            present=False
    OwnershipLost        present=False
    StaleWrite           present=False
    WriteRejected        present=False

  BaseCheckpointSaver.aput return annotation:
